<title>HONG KONG: Paliburg Holdings 1996 net up 73.58 pct.</title>
<headline>Paliburg Holdings 1996 net up 73.58 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  35.7	 vs 20.4</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   11.8	 vs 9.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 117.4 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			   670.0	vs 386.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		    4,335.2    vs 3,246.4</p>
<p>    Company name		Paliburg Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 June 12-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  July 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Paliburg Holdings is a property development concern.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-four shares held.</p>
<p>The exceptional items in 1996 represent the profits of HK$75.9 million and HK$41.5 million respectively derived from disposals of certain investment properties and share investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 15 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 3.2 cents) vs 12 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
